cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HYBRID-MH: a bias-controlled MH sampler for criticality in LLM multi-agent systems"
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Sorrowa"
    # Replace with your real name / affiliation / ORCID before citing.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sorrowa/llm-cooperative-criticality"
abstract: >-
  HYBRID-MH uses an LLM as the proposal distribution in a Metropolis-Hastings
  chain against a pre-registered Ising target Hamiltonian, dividing out the
  agent's intrinsic bias so that the chain samples the cooperative target by
  detailed balance. Under this control the finite-size-scaling exponent on a 2D
  lattice is statistically consistent with the 2D-Ising value (no new
  universality class), while the framework retains discriminating power across
  interaction topologies. Includes a classical-Ising control, raw chains, and a
  full self-audit / retraction trail.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - multi-agent systems
  - phase transitions
  - Metropolis-Hastings
  - Ising model
  - finite-size scaling
license: MIT
